[manifest]
display_name="i915-sriov-dkms"
desc="Intel i915-sriov-dkms graphics driver<br>Restart the system after installation or removal for changes to take effect.<br>For enabling SR-IOV on Intel UHD 7XX integrated graphics on the host so virtual machines can use virtual functions.<br>Issues caused by running fnOS inside a virtual machine are not currently supported, but feedback is welcome. Consumer discrete GPUs such as DG1 are not currently supported for SR-IOV.<br>After installing and configuring the driver, create VFs with:<br><code>echo 3 &gt; /sys/devices/pci0000:00/0000:00:02.0/sriov_numvfs</code><br>When passing through a VF, take care not to pass through the PF. See the upstream project documentation for configuration details.<br><br>Prebuilt kernel modules included by default:<br>6.18.18.c788-trim, 6.18.18.c877-trim, 6.18.18.c938-trim, 6.18.18.c952-trim, 6.18.18.c1032-trim, 6.18.18.c1078-trim, 6.18.18.c1126-trim, 6.18.18.c1168-trim.<br><br>Archived builds for unsupported old kernels (excluded by default; included only when the old-kernel build option is enabled):<br>6.6.38-trim #92, 6.12.5-trim #10, 6.12.18-trim #3, 6.18.6-trim #297, 6.18.18-trim #427, #570, #587, #717.<br><br>If no prebuilt module matches the current kernel, the installation wizard can allow a local chroot build as a fallback. This carries higher risk; waiting for a prebuilt release is recommended.<br><br>This driver is provided and maintained by community users. Report issues directly to community users and include the exported logs."
changelog="Updated upstream DKMS to 2026.09.16 and i915 firmware to Xe3LPD DMC v2.36. Added Chinese and English app information and installation messages, and archived kernels without a .c build suffix as unsupported old kernels."

[wizard]
install_step_title="Kernel module installation"
install_mode_label="Choose an installation method"
prebuilt_only_label="Use prebuilt modules only (recommended)"
allow_local_build_label="Allow a local build when missing (high risk, not recommended)"
local_build_warning="<strong>Warning: We strongly recommend using prebuilt modules only and waiting for a release that supports your kernel.</strong><br><br>Local builds are intended only for advanced users who can diagnose and accept kernel-driver risks. Build time depends on the system configuration; closely monitor system resource usage while compilation is running. Compilation may saturate CPU, memory, and disk I/O for an extended period, causing severe slowdowns, interrupted services, or an unresponsive system.<br><br>The resulting module has not been pre-validated and may fail to load or destabilize the system, potentially requiring a restart."

